.TH timebook 1 2026-11-19 "sandogasa 0.28.2" "Sandogasa Manual"
.SH NAME
timebook \- Find free Fedora meeting rooms and check bookings in Fedora Calendar
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtimebook\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fedora\*(Aqs shared meeting rooms (meeting, meeting\-1, ...) as Fedora Calendar books them: which rooms a planned meeting, or a series of them, would find free, and what each room holds.
.PP
A calendar entry\*(Aqs location is free text, so one room appears under many names (meeting\-1@chat.fedoraproject.org, a matrix.to link, the IRC channel it replaced); timebook reads them all as the room. Times are compared in UTC.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH COMMANDS
.SS timebook cancel
\fBtimebook cancel\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-meeting\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fICALENDAR|ENTRY\fR> <\fIDATES\fR>
.PP
Cancel occurrences of one of your own meetings
.PP
Takes the occurrences on the days given off Fedora Calendar, past or coming: a meeting that was not held, or will not be. Logs in with your Kerberos ticket (fkinit), lists the occurrences and cancels them once you confirm, checking each is gone. fedocal cancels one occurrence of a series by ending it the day before and starting it again, as a new entry, after it.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Log in and list the occurrences, but cancel nothing
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-meeting\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
Part of the title of the meeting meant, in a calendar with several
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Cancel without asking
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fICALENDAR|ENTRY\fR>
The meeting\*(Aqs calendar, or the id or page of one of its entries
.TP
<\fIDATES\fR>
The days to cancel (YYYY\-MM\-DD, the meeting\*(Aqs own date)
.SS timebook check
\fBtimebook check\fR [\fB\-\-count\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-every\fR] [\fB\-\-minutes\fR] [\fB\-\-suggest\fR] [\fB\-\-tz\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIROOM\fR> <\fIAT\fR>
.PP
Check whether a room is free for a planned meeting or series
.TP
\fB\-\-count\fR \fI<COUNT>\fR [default: 1]
How many meetings in the series (1 to 520)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-every\fR \fI<EVERY>\fR [default: 7]
Days between meetings (1 to 366)
.TP
\fB\-\-minutes\fR \fI<MINUTES>\fR [default: 60]
How long each meeting is, in minutes (1 to 1440)
.TP
\fB\-\-suggest\fR
Check whether the meetings in a taken room still take place
.TP
\fB\-\-tz\fR \fI<TZ>\fR [default: UTC]
The time zone of AT, e.g. Europe/Dublin
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIROOM\fR>
The room: meeting, meeting\-1, or any name of it
.TP
<\fIAT\fR>
When the first one starts: YYYY\-MM\-DD HH:MM, in \-\-tz
.SS timebook edit
\fBtimebook edit\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-location\fR] [\fB\-\-note\fR] [\fB\-\-title\fR] [\fB\-\-until\fR] [\fB\-\-meeting\fR] [\fB\-\-one\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fICALENDAR|ENTRY\fR>
.PP
Change one of your own calendar entries
.PP
Logs in to Fedora Calendar with your Kerberos ticket (fkinit), reads the entry, shows each change before and after, and saves it once you confirm, reading it back. For a recurring entry the whole series changes from its next occurrence on, fedocal keeping the earlier ones as a separate entry; \-\-one changes that occurrence alone.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fICALENDAR|ENTRY\fR>
The entry: its id or page (.../meeting/<id>/), or its meeting\*(Aqs calendar, for the entry of its next occurrence
.SH CHANGES
.TP
\fB\-\-location\fR \fI<LOCATION>\fR
Where it takes place, e.g. a room or a public video link
.TP
\fB\-\-note\fR \fI<NOTE>\fR
Its description
.TP
\fB\-\-title\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
Its title
.TP
\fB\-\-until\fR \fI<UNTIL>\fR
The last day a series repeats on (YYYY\-MM\-DD)
.SH SELECTION
.TP
\fB\-\-meeting\fR \fI<TITLE>\fR
Part of the title of the meeting meant, in a calendar with several
.TP
\fB\-\-one\fR
Change only the next occurrence of a series
.SH WRITING
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Log in and show the changes, but save nothing
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Save without asking
.SS timebook find
\fBtimebook find\fR [\fB\-\-count\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-every\fR] [\fB\-\-minutes\fR] [\fB\-\-suggest\fR] [\fB\-\-tz\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIAT\fR>
.PP
Find the rooms free for a planned meeting or series
.PP
When no room is free for every meeting, or with \-\-suggest, the meetings in the taken rooms are looked up in meetbot: a room whose meetings have had no minutes in the last 12 weeks is shown as likely free, with the evidence.
.TP
\fB\-\-count\fR \fI<COUNT>\fR [default: 1]
How many meetings in the series (1 to 520)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-every\fR \fI<EVERY>\fR [default: 7]
Days between meetings (1 to 366)
.TP
\fB\-\-minutes\fR \fI<MINUTES>\fR [default: 60]
How long each meeting is, in minutes (1 to 1440)
.TP
\fB\-\-suggest\fR
Check whether the meetings in a taken room still take place
.TP
\fB\-\-tz\fR \fI<TZ>\fR [default: UTC]
The time zone of AT, e.g. Europe/Dublin
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIAT\fR>
When the first one starts: YYYY\-MM\-DD HH:MM, in \-\-tz
.SS timebook rooms
\fBtimebook rooms\fR [\fB\-\-days\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-from\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
List what each room holds in a period
.TP
\fB\-\-days\fR \fI<DAYS>\fR [default: 28]
Days to cover (1 to 366)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-from\fR \fI<FROM>\fR
First day (YYYY\-MM\-DD; default today)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SS timebook stale
\fBtimebook stale\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-refresh\fR] [\fB\-\-weeks\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
Check whether recurring meetings still take place
.PP
Each recurring entry of the last weeks is looked for in meetbot\*(Aqs minutes (by its calendar\*(Aqs name and its title as a topic), an occurrence counting as held when minutes in its room start within an hour of it. For a series without any, its owners\*(Aq last activity on Discourse is shown; for one held at least sometimes, the days without minutes are listed with the `timebook cancel` command that takes them off (the last day only with \-\-refresh, as meetbot\*(Aqs answers are kept for a day). Series that stopped at 2025\-12\-31, fedocal\*(Aqs old default end for a series without one, are listed with any minutes since: those may still be held.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print JSON instead of text
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\fR
Ask meetbot again instead of using answers from the last day
.TP
\fB\-\-weeks\fR \fI<WEEKS>\fR [default: 12]
Weeks back to look (1 to 52)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
